# Documentation lives in two places, always in sync

Every piece of project documentation must exist in **both** this repository and the
Notion Project Knowledge Library, and both copies must be updated in the same turn.

- Notion library: https://app.notion.com/p/7cc641cb90c1408d9419894d90233c7b
  (data source `collection://f0c83c93-62b6-4e7a-a0e3-3f6d687bc220`)
- Sync index (source of the mapping): [`docs/notion-sync.md`](../../docs/notion-sync.md)

## Where things go

| Content | Repository | Notion |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reference docs (architecture, application guide, student guide, sample data) | `README.md`, `docs/*.md`, `data/samples/README.md` | Page in the library, Type = Reference / How-to |
| Session summaries, decisions, research findings | `docs/notes/YYYY-MM-DD-<subject>.md` | Page in the library, Type = Session summary / Decision / Research |
| Mapping between the two | `docs/notion-sync.md` | `Repo mirror:` line on each Notion page |

## Rules

1. Creating or editing a Notion page for this project → write or update the matching
   file under `docs/notes/` (or the matching reference doc) and add/refresh the row in
   `docs/notion-sync.md`. Commit it together with any code change.
2. Creating or editing `README.md`, anything in `docs/`, or `data/samples/README.md` →
   update the corresponding Notion page in the same turn (create it if missing, and
   add it to `docs/notion-sync.md`).
3. Every Notion page for this project carries a `Repo mirror:` line with the repo path.
4. Never leave one side stale. If a sync cannot be completed (Notion unavailable, no
   push access), say so explicitly in the summary and record it as an Open follow-up
   in both places once reachable.
5. Mirrors are content-equivalent, not necessarily byte-identical: convert Notion
   headings/callouts to Markdown, keep the same sections (Outcome, Key decisions,
   Artifacts/links, Open follow-ups), and keep dates and decision wording unchanged.
